\page versioning Versioning

Nocterm follows [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/) (`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH[-PRERELEASE]`). The current version of the project is tracked in a single `VERSION` file at the root of the repository.

When the project is configured (Refer to \ref installation), this version is parsed and used to generate a header file `nocterm/version.h`, which is placed alongside the other installed headers.

---

# API Overview

To access version information at compile time, include the generated header:

```c
#include <nocterm/version.h>
```

The header defines the following macros:

| Macro                          | Description                                              |
| ------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |
| `NOCTERM_VERSION_MAJOR`          | Major version number                                       |
| `NOCTERM_VERSION_MINOR`          | Minor version number                                       |
| `NOCTERM_VERSION_PATCH`          | Patch version number                                       |
| `NOCTERM_VERSION_PRERELEASE`     | Pre-release identifier (e.g. `alpha.1`), if any            |
| `NOCTERM_VERSION`                | Full version string (e.g. `"1.0.0-alpha.1"`)               |

`Example`

```c
#include <nocterm/nocterm.h>
#include <nocterm/version.h>

int main(){

    nocterm_io_print("Built with Nocterm v%s\n", NOCTERM_VERSION);
    nocterm_io_print("Major version: %d\n", NOCTERM_VERSION_MAJOR);

    return 0;
}
```

> `NOCTERM_VERSION_PRERELEASE` is only meaningful when the project is built from a pre-release `VERSION` (i.e. one containing a `-` suffix). If there is no pre-release suffix, this macro expands to an empty string `""`.

